  "holes": [
    "A record of her own (`lore.file` and its three side files). Her material is her bible, her speech guide and her structured sheet; no records.json, triggers.json, memories.json or memory_triggers.json has been built from them, so `lore` is left at its default (off) and she retrieves nothing. This is the first thing to author before she is worth talking to for long.",
    "Her household (`household.file`, the things in her flat), her home (`world.home_file`) and her own day beyond the resident fallback. Tier 2 drops the world, the schedule and the body, so these are deliberately absent: `resident/app.py:plan_day` falls back to the one-block resident day.",
    "Her own people of any kind. Her record names 一悟 and the girls of her scenes, but they are people she remembers out of the game, not people in a day: she has no world, so they are not roster rows and no meter is seeded on them. The only person on her roster is him.",
    "Her gauge baselines of her own (`temperament.gauge_baselines`). None is authored from her material yet; the library's defaults stand. Not a defect at boot, but her temperament is not yet hers."
  ],
